FAQ = [
 ("Do Denali and AT4 Sierras need special floor liners?",
  "No. The Denali, AT4, AT4X, Elevation, SLT and SLE Crew Cabs share the T1 cab floor, so the fit rules are the same as any Crew Cab: match the front seats and the rear under-seat storage. Denali and AT4 trucks almost always have front buckets with a console, which narrows the choice to bucket-seat liners. Some listings name trims; if yours does not, it's the layout that counts."),
 ("Can I use Silverado 1500 liners in a Sierra 1500?",
  "Yes. The two trucks share the Crew Cab body and floor, and most of the listings on this page name both. Husky's 94021, the 3W, KUST and Falafa sets are all listed for Silverado and Sierra together. The OMAC and TuxMat sets on this page are Sierra-specific listings, but the same makers sell matching Silverado versions."),
 ("What's the difference between TuxMat and a regular liner?",
  "Coverage. TuxMat says its mats are laser-scanned and extend up the sidewalls to protect areas other mats leave exposed, with a textured, leather-like surface. They are also the most expensive set on this page. A conventional liner like Husky's or a budget TPE set covers the footwell floor with raised walls. If you want the carpet behind the pedals and up the sides covered too, TuxMat is the premium route."),
 ("Which rear liner fits a Sierra with the under-seat storage box?",
  "One cut for the box. Crew Cab Sierras can have factory carpeted storage, a molded plastic storage box, or neither under the rear seat. Falafa and KUST sell sets listed for the storage box. Husky's 94021 is listed for carpet with underseat storage. Lift the rear cushion and compare with the listing photos before ordering."),
 ("Do these liners fit a 2022+ refreshed Sierra?",
  "The 2022 refresh changed the dash and moved the shifter to the console on most trims, but not the floor. OMAC runs 2019–2025 and TuxMat 2019–2026, and Husky's 94021 runs 2019–2025. The 2022 Sierra 1500 Limited is the carryover truck with the previous interior, and several makers list it separately."),
 ("Will a liner fit a Sierra Double Cab?",
  "Not the rear piece. All five picks here are Crew Cab sets. The Double Cab's rear floor is shorter. Front pairs are sometimes shared: Husky's 13211 front liners are listed for both Double and Crew Cab. Buy the rear liner specifically for the Double Cab."),
 ("Is OMAC a good brand?",
  "OMAC sells custom-fit TPE liners at budget prices, and its listing here is Sierra-specific, which is a point in its favor. We could not find a published warranty or cold rating from OMAC to compare, so we rank it on the fit it claims and the price. If you want written terms, Husky and TuxMat publish lifetime warranties."),
 ("How should floor liners sit around the pedals?",
  "Flat, locked onto the driver-side retention posts, and clear of the pedals at full travel. Remove the factory carpet mat before installing any liner. After fitting, push the driver liner forward with your heel; it shouldn't move. Then press the brake and accelerator to the floor and make sure neither touches the liner edge."),
 ("Do I need a liner for the center floor on a bench-seat Sierra?",
  "If you carry a third passenger up front, yes. On a bench-seat Sierra the middle of the front floor sits between the two footwells, and two-piece front liners usually stop at the edge of each footwell. Mud from the middle passenger's boots lands on that strip of carpet. Some makers sell the front row as a one-piece bench liner or add a center hump piece; Husky, for example, sells center hump pieces for other GM and Ram trucks. Ask the seller whether their bench layout covers the middle before ordering."),
 ("What's the easiest way to clean them?",
  "Pull them, rinse with a hose, scrub with mild soap and let them dry. TuxMat's textured surface wipes clean with a damp cloth for light dirt. Avoid silicone protectants on any liner, because they make the surface slippery under wet boots."),
]

